      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Mountain instead of Thundering Falls on turn 1 is suboptimal. Thundering Falls enters tapped, so playing it on turn 1 (when you want to cast Ragavan on turn 1 anyway but can't off Thundering Falls) means you lose nothing by playing it now and having it untapped on turn 2. However, the key issue is that playing Mountain turn 1 enables casting Ragavan turn 1 (which is the best play in Modern), so Mountain is actually correct IF you plan to cast Ragavan this turn. But wait - looking at the hand, the player HAS Ragavan and Mountain produces R, so playing Mountain and casting Ragavan turn 1 is the right line. The question is whether the player will follow through with casting Ragavan. If they do, Mountain is correct. If they play Thundering Falls instead, they'd lose the tempo of a turn 1 Ragavan. Actually, Mountain is the correct play here to enable turn 1 Ragavan, so this is not a blunder.",
