      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "With Eldrazi Temple untapped, Gem25F Coach could cast Kozilek's Command for X=0 (cost {C}{C} paid by Eldrazi Temple for an Eldrazi spell), choosing 'scry 0 then draw a card' as one mode, effectively cycling their last card for free. At 8 life with no creatures and no board presence, drawing into an answer could be critical.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without casting Kozilek's Command, saving it for a future turn with more mana.",
      "better_line": "Cast Kozilek's Command for X=0 using Eldrazi Temple, choosing 'scry 0, draw a card' and 'exile up to 0 cards from graveyards' to cycle into a potentially game-saving card. Alternatively, saving for a bigger X is defensible if they expect to untap with more mana, but the urgency of their position argues for drawing now.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 135,
      "player": "Gem25F Coach",
      "decision_index": 206,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Solitude before playing Arid Mesa as their land for the turn. Playing Arid Mesa first and potentially fetching a land would have preserved the Treasure Token or provided better mana options. The sequencing of casting spells before making land drops is a clear error, though the impact here is modest since the Treasure Token was consumed for mana.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Solitude using Treasure Token before playing Arid Mesa as land drop",
      "better_line": "Play Arid Mesa first, crack it to fetch a Plains or other white source, then cast Solitude using the additional land instead of the Treasure Token, preserving the Treasure for future use",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 137,
      "player": "MiMo Villain",
      "decision_index": 209,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With an empty hand and needing to find relevant cards, Elegant Parlor's surveil 1 would help improve draw quality. Sacred Foundry provides color flexibility but they already have adequate color coverage (Mountain, Meticulous Archive for red; Plains, Hallowed Fountain for white). The surveil is more impactful in this top-deck mode.",
      "action_taken": "Fetched Sacred Foundry, providing R/W dual but costing 2 life to enter untapped or entering tapped with no additional benefit.",
      "better_line": "Fetch Elegant Parlor to get the surveil 1 trigger, improving draw quality while empty-handed. It enters tapped but provides the same R/W colors, and the card selection is more valuable than having an untapped land with nothing to cast.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 145,
      "player": "MiMo Villain",
      "decision_index": 220,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Gem25F Coach declined to cast Kozilek's Command despite having sufficient mana (6 available including Eldrazi Temple's {C}{C} for Eldrazi spells) and it being their only card in hand. With X=4, they could create 4 Eldrazi Spawn tokens and scry 4 + draw a card, generating significant board presence and card advantage. There's no reason to hold this spell with an empty hand and no better timing consideration.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without casting Kozilek's Command, leaving all mana unused with an empty hand after.",
      "better_line": "Cast Kozilek's Command for X=4, choosing to create 4 Eldrazi Spawn tokens and scry 4 + draw a card, generating board presence and card advantage in a topdecking situation.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 160,
      "player": "Gem25F Coach",
      "decision_index": 243,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Failed to cast Kozilek's Command at end of opponent's turn with plenty of mana available and only one card in hand. Could have cast it for X=4 (using Eldrazi Temple's {C}{C} for the colorless Eldrazi cost), choosing 'scry 4, draw a card' plus 'create 4 Spawn tokens' or 'exile up to 4 graveyard cards'. This would have provided significant card advantage and board presence at instant speed with no downside to waiting.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, wasting all available mana at end of opponent's turn",
      "better_line": "Cast Kozilek's Command for X=4 at end of opponent's turn, choosing 'scry 4, draw a card' and 'create 4 Eldrazi Spawn tokens' to generate card advantage and board presence",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 162,
      "player": "Gem25F Coach",
      "decision_index": 246,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "In a topdeck situation with empty hand, chose Inquisition of Kozilek as the topmost card to draw next. Hand disruption is weak when you need board presence to close out the game against an opponent at 10 life with no creatures. The opponent may also have few cards in hand at this stage.",
      "action_taken": "Put Inquisition of Kozilek on top of library to draw next turn",
      "better_line": "Put Thought-Knot Seer on top to draw next - it provides a 4/4 body to pressure the opponent's 10 life total while also stripping a card, and Eldrazi Temple helps cast it. Emperor of Bones would also be a strong alternative for immediate board impact.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 167,
      "player": "Gem25F Coach",
      "decision_index": 257,
    }
  ],
